        card("Activity 8, passage 1: a conversation between relatives (the book’s script and key)", "Key: 1. she lost her luggage at the airport and asks her aunt for help or does not know what to do; 2. the caller and her daughter or son; 3. Romeo Magtalas is the aunt’s godson at his wedding, works at the lost and found section of NAIA, and was referred to by the aunt to help the caller.", examples=dlg(_L1)),
        card("Activity 8, passage 2: a traveler and an immigration officer (the book’s script and key)", "Key: 4. the passport expires on December 20 (the book adds 2018, which is not in the script); 5. the officer asked for additional identification, the length of stay, whether the traveler has a relative in the Philippines and where he will live; 6. passport, driver’s license and company ID; 7. he has a house in the Philippines and his wife and children live there.", examples=dlg(_L2)),
        card("Activity 9: siblings talking about travel plans (the book’s script and key)", "Key: 1. the sister was invited to be bridesmaid at Aby’s wedding and asks her brother to pay for her plane ticket to Manila; 2. the brother’s reminders are to make sure she has a valid passport, not to bring plenty of luggage and to check whether a storm is coming; 3. she will stay in Manila for four days, fly to Manila on Friday, attend the wedding on Sunday morning and fly back to San Francisco on Sunday night. The book’s script misprints the brother’s last question as Ilang raw ka ba; the sensible reading is Ilang araw ka ba.", examples=dlg(_L3)),
        card("Activity 10: a voicemail (the book’s script and key)", "Key: Gloria, Georgina’s godmother, left a voicemail. She did not know right away that Georgina is going home to the Philippines and would have bought presents for Georgina’s siblings. She asks Georgina to drop by her house to get money to buy the presents, and will also send the land title and marriage certificate through Georgina, to be given to Gloria’s brother in the Philippines.", examples=passage(_VM)),
